{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars","id":610795,"title":"Directional and elemental associations of the Solars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-01T07:32:06-07:00","id":610795,"title":"Directional and elemental associations of the Solars","content":"Why don't the directional and elemental caste associations of the Solar Exalted match up? On the map of Creation, the Elemental Pole of Earth is in the center, Air is in the north, Wood in the east, Fire in the south, and Water in the west. Yet, the Dawn caste is associated with fire and the east; Zeniths with earth and the south; Twilights with wood and the west; Nights with water and the north; Eclipses with air and the center. Is this just an error, to be corrected in 3E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1856-hakkonen","name":"Hakkonen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:49:42-07:00","id":610832,"title":"","content":"All of the Caste associations are like that. They're not intended to match, though I would be surprised if they didn't match up for Dragon-Blooded Aspects.<br /> <br /> What does bug me is the way the Sidereal Castes are associated with Summer, Winter, Fall, Spring, and Calibration, instead of the seasons that actually exist in Creation (Water, Earth, Fire, Wood, Air). Or at least that's how it's said on the Wiki.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:52:42-07:00","id":610835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610832#post610832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the Caste associations are like that. They're not intended to match, though I would be surprised if they didn't match up for Dragon-Blooded Aspects.<br /> <br /> What does bug me is the way the Sidereal Castes are associated with Summer, Winter, Fall, Spring, and Calibration, instead of the seasons that actually exist in Creation (Water, Earth, Fire, Wood, Air). Or at least that's how it's said on the Wiki.</div> </div> </div> </div>The non-elemental seasons do exist, though. Just because you give the season an elemental name on the official calendar doesn't actually mean that other designations aren't possible or valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T07:59:21-07:00","id":610838,"title":"","content":"But there are 5 seasons, not 4. Having 4 Castes associated with only some of seasons, then skipping the 5th season and putting the 5th Caste with Calibration instead, doesn't make sense. It's almost as silly as saying &quot;spring, summer, autumn, Calibration, Tuesday.&quot; Or &quot;Mercuryday, Venusday, Marsday, Jupiterday, Sunday.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T08:45:57-07:00","id":610904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hakkonen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars#post610795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this just an error, to be corrected in 3E?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're reading waaaaaaaay too deep into flavor text.<br /> <br /> In any case those associations make sense to me. East is a heavily populated direction full of diverse populations in proximity, leading to lots of skirmishes. The south requires fortitude and survival skills to live and further is a landscape blasted by the Sun which makes it appropriate for his priests to be associated with it. Nights and the North could play into the insidious ways that cold can defeat you before you realize it, or the concealment of blizzard. The center is the direction of rulership, court, and civilization, hence Eclipses. I got nothing for the Twilight. The west is mysterious and full of hidden secrets they can reveal or something. <br /> <br /> Fire destroys like the Dawn. Earth is stoic and centered like the Zenith. Wood grows, like knowledge and the Twilight. Water can get anywhere like there the Night. Air permeates and connects everything like the Eclipse. <br /> <br /> These were all easy things I just came up with, so...see first paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-01-2015, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T09:15:35-07:00","id":610920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610838#post610838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are 5 seasons, not 4. Having 4 Castes associated with only some of seasons, then skipping the 5th season and putting the 5th Caste with Calibration instead, doesn't make sense. It's almost as silly as saying &quot;spring, summer, autumn, Calibration, Tuesday.&quot; Or &quot;Mercuryday, Venusday, Marsday, Jupiterday, Sunday.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to say that the Elemental Seasons are a Realm (or Old Realm) Calendar thing, and not an actual seasonal divide thing.<br /> <br /> I mean, we have 4 seasons here on earth (marked by the Equinoxes/Solstices) but the actual dates don't mean anything regarding snowfall (It seems we've always had at least one snowfall in Chicago that stayed overnight before my birthday at the end of November. This past year we had snow on Halloween.) or when plants bloom (those crocuses don't wait for the first day of Spring to start pushing through the snow) or when the birds migrate. In a temperate climate, the seasons are Cold, Cold-turning-Warm, Warm, and Warm-turning-cold. In more tropical climates the seasons are Wet and Dry (or Wet and Not-so-wet)<br /> <br /> And I seem to recall (though I can't find it now) that the seasons of Planting, Growth, Harvest, and Dormancy don't actually match up on a 1:1 basis with the five seasons. I know people try to get 2-3 harvests in, so I guess there's a Harvest and Harvest 2, but those aren't really separate seasons, weather wise.<br /> <br /> As for the days of the week... I thought they were Sunday Moonday, Marsday, Mercuryday, Venusday, Jupiterday (Just like I'm pretty sure the English Calendar's days are derived from Sun day Moon Day, Tiw's Day, Woden's Day, Thor's Day, Freyr's day and Saturn's Day.) Though the days of the week even having specific names may be fanon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":424,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","user":"DaWaterRat","date":". 08-01-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T09:48:32-07:00","id":610964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610904#post610904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">East is a heavily populated direction full of diverse populations in proximity, leading to lots of skirmishes. [...] I got nothing for the Twilight. The west is mysterious and full of hidden secrets they can reveal or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Or</i>, they're just the Directions where the sun rises and sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:30:02-07:00","id":611047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610964#post610964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Or</i>, they're just the Directions where the sun rises and sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's much more sensical but also hella boring. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T10:33:33-07:00","id":611050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610964#post610964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Or</i>, they're just the Directions where the sun rises and sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's this. The sun rises in the east - that's where the dawn happens. Zenith is south because in the real life earth's northern hemisphere (where most humans, including the authors, live), the sun is in the south at midday. In creation, it might be closer to the south, too, if you don't want to attribute all of the temperature to the elemental pole of fire. Then, again, west is where the sun sets, hence, twilight. The sun is never seen north, unless you're living in the southern hemisphere of real life's earth, hence that's the Night Caste. Last but not least, the Eclypse gets what's left and what connects everything.<br /> <br /> I'm with Zelbinnean on the elemental associations, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","user":"Dusk Shine","date":". 08-01-2015, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1313-dusk-shine","name":"Dusk Shine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1313_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"256"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:36:17-07:00","id":611105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there are 5 seasons, not 4.</div> </div> </div> </div> Four non-elemental seasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T13:58:53-07:00","id":611323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610920#post610920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the days of the week... I thought they were Sunday Moonday, Marsday, Mercuryday, Venusday, Jupiterday (Just like I'm pretty sure the English Calendar's days are derived from Sun day Moon Day, Tiw's Day, Woden's Day, Thor's Day, Freyr's day and Saturn's Day.) Though the days of the week even having specific names may be fanon.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not fanon, it was in Lunars 2e, page 229. TGIV!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T17:27:25-07:00","id":611490,"title":"","content":"You forgot Saturnday.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T21:30:11-07:00","id":611866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/610795-directional-and-elemental-associations-of-the-solars?p=610920#post610920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the days of the week... I thought they were Sunday Moonday, Marsday, Mercuryday, Venusday, Jupiterday (Just like I'm pretty sure the English Calendar's days are derived from Sun day Moon Day, Tiw's Day, Woden's Day, Thor's Day, Freyr's day and Saturn's Day.) Though the days of the week even having specific names may be fanon.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Savage Seas</i> had a demon who didn't like Venus' Day. And there was an additional referency to Thursday in <i>Castebook: Twilight</i>, so it's not actually that odd.<br /> <br /> The order of days in the week is originally from Babylonian stuff if I remember right, got to India and then spread out to everywehre else. It is indeed the root words as yo note for the seven days based on seven planets. In East Asia, they use the elemental associations, but since the planets are just &quot;Element Star&quot;, for instnace, even though Fireday is what Tuesday typically translates to, it's still Tuesday since it's about the Fire Star, aka, Mars, aka, Tiw.<br /> <br /> It became for reals canon in <i>MoEP: Lunars</i>, but some things of that might not stick. Calibration being starless is a 2e invention, for instnace, and the 25 hour day is just plain awkward to work with and is cute for cute's sake I think.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}